# A Red Flag in the White House!
Tamil title: வெள்ளை மாளிகையில் சிகப்புக் கொடி!

A campaign to defeat the capitalists.

The peerless man’s tireless labour.

Opposition broken! Conspiracy defeated!

A great warrior who died while plucking a flower.

Roosevelt’s heroic life.

“The story is over!” Roosevelt’s wife said as she came out of the White House. Those were the words that burst forth from that grief-laden heart: “The story is over!” Yes, it had indeed ended: the story of the unshaken hero; a fascinating story in American history; a story that moves the hearts of the people of the world. It had indeed ended! Yet what a rare and extraordinary story it was!

Born in 1882.

Graduated in 1903.

Married in 1905.

Began practising law in 1905.

Won election to the Senate in 1910.

Became Assistant Secretary of the Navy in 1913.

Fell into the sea in 1921 and was stricken with paralysis.

Became Governor of New York in 1928.

Became Governor of New York again in 1930.

Became President in 1933!

---NOTES---
The available scan ends after the chronology and is evidently the opening page of a longer article. The years and several damaged words were verified against the printed scan.
